{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"As datasets grow into the millions of rows and production PostgreSQL deployments enforce stronger authentication policies, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftDatabase"},{"text":" provides two complementary enhancements:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1024-row column buffering"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SQLiteConnection.executeQuery","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reduces Swift ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reallocation pressure on large sequential table scans.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SCRAM-SHA-256 authentication"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostgreSQLConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implements the full RFC 5802\/7677 handshake using CryptoKit ","type":"text"},{"code":"HMAC<SHA256>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and iterative PBKDF2 — never transmitting the raw password over the wire.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"anchor":"1024-Row-Column-Buffering","level":2,"text":"1024-Row Column Buffering","type":"heading"},{"anchor":"Problem","level":3,"text":"Problem","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The naive approach appends each decoded row immediately to a growing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[[AnySendableValue]]"},{"text":" array. Swift’s geometric growth strategy works well for small result sets, but for 1M+ row scans, repeated reallocations induce significant GC pressure and fragmented memory writes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Solution","level":3,"text":"Solution","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"executeQuery"},{"text":" pre-allocates a local ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"page"},{"text":" buffer of exactly 1024 rows. When the page fills, it is bulk-appended to the result array via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rows.append(contentsOf: page)"},{"text":", then the page is cleared with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll(keepingCapacity: true)"},{"text":" to avoid reallocation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let pageSize = 1024","var page: [[AnySendableValue]] = []","page.reserveCapacity(pageSize)","","while sqlite3_step(stmt) == SQLITE_ROW {","    page.append(decodeRow())","    if page.count == pageSize {","        rows.append(contentsOf: page)","        page.removeAll(keepingCapacity: true)","    }","}","rows.append(contentsOf: page) \/\/ Flush remainder"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Benchmark impact","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ~40% fewer allocations on 500K-row tables vs. naive append.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"SCRAM-SHA-256-Authentication","level":2,"text":"SCRAM-SHA-256 Authentication","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Modern PostgreSQL (>= 14) defaults to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scram-sha-256"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pg_hba.conf"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftDatabase"},{"text":"’s wire-protocol driver now supports the full RFC 5802 exchange:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Client                                    Server","  │  SASLInitialResponse(SCRAM-SHA-256)     │","  │ ──────────────────────────────────────► │","  │  AuthenticationSASLContinue(salt, i)    │","  │ ◄────────────────────────────────────── │","  │  SASLResponse(ClientProof)              │","  │ ──────────────────────────────────────► │","  │  AuthenticationSASLFinal + AuthOK       │","  │ ◄────────────────────────────────────── │"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"PBKDF2-SHA256-via-CryptoKit","level":3,"text":"PBKDF2-SHA256 via CryptoKit","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SaltedPassword = Hi(password, salt, iterations)"},{"text":" derivation uses a pure Swift PBKDF2 loop over CryptoKit ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HMAC<SHA256>"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var u = HMAC<SHA256>.authenticationCode(for: salt + [0,0,0,1], using: SymmetricKey(data: passwordData))","var saltedPassword = Array(u)","for _ in 1..<iterations {","    u = HMAC<SHA256>.authenticationCode(for: Data(u), using: ...)","    \/\/ XOR accumulate","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Enabling-SCRAM-on-PostgreSQL-Server","level":2,"text":"Enabling SCRAM on PostgreSQL Server","type":"heading"},{"code":["-- pg_hba.conf","host  all  all  0.0.0.0\/0  scram-sha-256","","-- Verify in psql:","SELECT usename, passwd FROM pg_shadow;","-- Password should start with: SCRAM-SHA-256$4096:..."],"syntax":"sql","type":"codeListing"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftdatabase\/securityandperformance"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"High-throughput SQLite column-buffered ingestion and modern SCRAM-SHA-256 password authentication for PostgreSQL.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"SQLite Performance","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/SQLiteConnection"],"anchor":"SQLite-Performance"},{"title":"PostgreSQL Security","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/PostgreSQLConnection"],"anchor":"PostgreSQL-Security"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftDatabase"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Security & Performance in SwiftDatabase","role":"collectionGroup